CBMC did not declare the implicit operator== of a class with a defaulted
operator<=> ([class.compare.default]/4): `a == b' was rejected with "no
comparison operator for an operand of class type", as `a != c' (which
[over.match.oper]/3.4 rewrites to !(a == c)).
